From: Cargt <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: stm32: use gpiod_set_value_cansleep() for reset GPIO

stm32_pcie_start_link()/stop_link() use gpiod_set_value(), which
gpiolib only permits on GPIO chips that cannot sleep. On boards where
"reset-gpios" is provided by an I2C-backed GPIO expander (e.g.
pca9555), every access blocks on an I2C transaction, so the chip is
marked can_sleep and this trips WARN_ON(chip->can_sleep) in
gpiod_set_value() (gpiolib.c) on every probe:

  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 440 at drivers/gpio/gpiolib.c:3309 gpiod_set_value+0x40/0xa4
  lr : stm32_pcie_start_link+0x28/0x8c [pcie_stm32]

We are always called from process context here (probe/remove), so
switch to the sleeping-safe variant.

Signed-off-by: Cargt <tim.carney@cargt.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-stm32.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-stm32.c
index 96976d8c5..1111111111 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-stm32.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-stm32.c
@@ -79,11 +79,11 @@
 
 	if (stm32_pcie->reset_gpio) {
 		/* Make sure PERST# is asserted. */
-		gpiod_set_value(stm32_pcie->reset_gpio, 1);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(stm32_pcie->reset_gpio, 1);
 
 		/* Deassert PERST# after 100us */
 		usleep_range(100, 200);
-		gpiod_set_value(stm32_pcie->reset_gpio, 0);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(stm32_pcie->reset_gpio, 0);
 	}
 
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(stm32_pcie->regmap, SYSCFG_PCIECR,
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@
 
 	/* Assert PERST# */
 	if (stm32_pcie->reset_gpio)
-		gpiod_set_value(stm32_pcie->reset_gpio, 1);
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(stm32_pcie->reset_gpio, 1);
 }
 
 static int stm32_pcie_suspend(struct device *dev)
